From 8f13328622ec2bdc19b96c9b7a3e7173a4b68096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:41:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cast: Implement remote playback control requests

Cast routes advertise the MediaControlIntent remote playback actions
(PLAY, SEEK, GET_STATUS, PAUSE, RESUME, STOP and the session actions),
but the route controller rejected every control request, so apps using
RemotePlaybackClient could select a Cast route and then not play on it.

Handle them on the Default Media Receiver: PLAY attaches to (or
launches) CC1AD845 on the route's CastV2 session and sends LOAD on the
media namespace; the other actions map to SEEK, GET_STATUS, PAUSE,
PLAY and STOP on the loaded media session. One remote playback session
with one item is kept, like the Default Media Receiver plays one item.
MEDIA_STATUS updates the item status, which is reported in the results
and through the status update receivers of the client, including the
end of playback and the receiver app being stopped or replaced. Ending
the session stops the receiver application.
